Step-by-Step Implementation Guide

Step 1: Provision Backend Node.js Applications
Log into your EC2 instance and create two lightweight, isolated Node.js applications:

# Create application directories
mkdir -p ~/app1 ~/app2

# App Instance 1 (Port 3001)
cat <<'EOF' > ~/app1/server.js
const http = require('http');
const PORT = 3001;

http.createServer((req, res) => {
  res.writeHead(200, { 'Content-Type': 'text/html' });
  res.end(`
    <div style="font-family: sans-serif; text-align: center; padding: 3rem; background: #0f172a; color: #38bdf8;">
      <h1>🟢 Backend App Instance 1</h1>
      <p>Served from internal port <strong>3001</strong></p>
    </div>
  `);
}).listen(PORT, () => console.log(`App 1 running on port ${PORT}`));
EOF

# App Instance 2 (Port 3002)
cat <<'EOF' > ~/app2/server.js
const http = require('http');
const PORT = 3002;

http.createServer((req, res) => {
  res.writeHead(200, { 'Content-Type': 'text/html' });
  res.end(`
    <div style="font-family: sans-serif; text-align: center; padding: 3rem; background: #0f172a; color: #a855f7;">
      <h1>🟣 Backend App Instance 2</h1>
      <p>Served from internal port <strong>3002</strong></p>
    </div>
  `);
}).listen(PORT, () => console.log(`App 2 running on port ${PORT}`));
EOF



Step 2: Manage Backend Daemons via PM2
Install pm2 globally to manage the backend node processes persistently:

# Install Node.js & PM2
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y nodejs npm
sudo npm install -g pm2

# Start both applications
pm2 start ~/app1/server.js --name "app-1"
pm2 start ~/app2/server.js --name "app-2"

# Verify execution status
pm2 list


Step 3: Configure Nginx Upstream Pool & Virtual Host
Create a new Nginx configuration file in sites-available:

sudo nano /etc/nginx/sites-available/load-balancer

Paste the following production load-balancer block:

# 1. Define Upstream Backend Application Pool
upstream node_backend_pool {
    # Round-Robin Balancing (Default) with Passive Health Checks
    server 127.0.0.1:3001 max_fails=3 fail_timeout=10s;
    server 127.0.0.1:3002 max_fails=3 fail_timeout=10s;
}

# 2. Virtual Host Edge Server
server {
    listen 80;
    listen [::]:80;

    server_name _;

    location / {
        # Forward ingress traffic to the upstream pool
        proxy_pass http://node_backend_pool;

        # Disable response caching for real-time load testing
        add_header Cache-Control "no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate, proxy-revalidate, max-age=0";
        proxy_hide_header Cache-Control;

        # Proxy Headers for preserving client metadata
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;

        # Timeout configurations
        proxy_connect_timeout 5s;
        proxy_read_timeout 60s;
    }
}


Step 4: Enable Site & Reload Nginx
Link the configuration, verify syntax, and reload Nginx:

# 1. Disable previous default/static sites if active
sudo rm -f /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/default
sudo rm -f /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/static-site

# 2. Enable load balancer configuration
sudo ln -sf /etc/nginx/sites-available/load-balancer /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/

# 3. Test configuration syntax
sudo nginx -t

# 4. Reload Nginx without dropping connections
sudo systemctl reload nginx



